    "totalDuration": "11 yrs 2 mos",
    "description": "I’ve worked at Google since September 2015 in teams focused on developer productivity and corporate accounting. In the past two years,\n• I created software to measure the impact of individual commits on Android app growth using multiple metrics. At the time of this writing, the analyzer was enabled for more than 240 targets Google-wide.\n• I led an effort to conduct a large-scale refactor of an Android app. In the process, I was able to design and implement algorithmic techniques that decreased my team’s workload by a factor of over 2x, along with tooling such that a similar effort could be replicated by any team in Google.\n• I migrated a central component of Gmail’s developer infrastructure onto production servers. The idea was to make it reusable by any team in Google. I resdesigned the database schema and logic, implemented production monitoring, and added application functionality.\n• I conceptualized, designed & implemented prototypes for a new corporate accounting system.\n• I worked to stabilize and add much-needed functionality to a legacy corporate accounting system.",
